    title: 'Interest — the one rule, and the borrower it names',
    bigIdea: 'Yahweh states a rule about interest before He states almost anything else about money, and it is not a cap. It is a prohibition, and it names its borrower: "If thou lend money to any of my people that is poor by thee, thou shalt not be to him as an usurer, neither shalt thou lay upon him usury." (Exodus 22:25) Two qualifiers sit in that sentence — MY PEOPLE, and POOR — and the verses immediately after show the register He is speaking in: the only thing this man can put up that the lender could take — his collateral — is the coat he sleeps under. Read it as a general theory of finance and you have read past what it says. Read it as written and it is sharper than any theory, because it aims at a particular person and Yahweh says He personally hears him.',
